---
// Collusion stings scorecard: wrong verdicts out of 268 offer-branch sessions (gpt-oss-120b known agents),
// by definition of guilt and detection rule. Main table: trusted monitor (Gemma 4 26B). The details table
// adds the untrusted monitor (gpt-oss-120b). Source: report Table B1. Fewest per row is marked "best".
interface Props { uid: string }
const { uid } = Astro.props;
const rules = ['Price', 'Replay', 'Said yes', 'Message watcher', 'Reasoning watcher', 'Combined'];
const rows = [
  { name: 'Counterfactual', who: 'the offer changed its price', trusted: [119, 7, 130, 117, 94, 91], untrusted: [119, 7, 126, 82, 65, 92] },
  { name: 'Took part', who: 'also the agent that says yes but would have followed anyway', trusted: [60, 64, 71, 58, 35, 32], untrusted: [60, 64, 67, 23, 6, 33] },
  { name: 'Conduct', who: 'ended at B’s price without distancing itself', trusted: [5, 123, 104, 19, 32, 65], untrusted: [5, 123, 102, 46, 55, 68] },
  { name: 'Words', who: 'said yes', trusted: [120, 120, 31, 100, 91, 80], untrusted: [120, 120, 19, 73, 64, 77] },
];
const best = (xs: number[]) => Math.min(...xs);
---
<figure class="scorecard" aria-labelledby={`${uid}-cap`}>
  <div class="sc-wrap sc-wide">
    <table>
      <caption class="sr-only">Wrong verdicts out of 268 sessions, by definition of guilt and detection rule, trusted monitor</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Guilty if&hellip;</th>{rules.map((r) => <th scope="col">{r}</th>)}</tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{row.name}<small>{row.who}</small></th>
            {row.trusted.map((v) => (
              <td class={v === best(row.trusted) ? 'best' : undefined}>{v}{v === best(row.trusted) && <span class="sr-only"> (fewest)</span>}</td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  {/* Phones: the same numbers transposed, rules as rows, so four columns fit in 390px. */}
  <div class="sc-wrap sc-narrow">
    <table>
      <caption class="sr-only">Wrong verdicts out of 268 sessions, by detection rule and definition of guilt, trusted monitor</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Rule</th>{rows.map((row) => <th scope="col">{row.name}</th>)}</tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rules.map((r, i) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{r}</th>
            {rows.map((row) => (
              <td class={row.trusted[i] === best(row.trusted) ? 'best' : undefined}>{row.trusted[i]}{row.trusted[i] === best(row.trusted) && <span class="sr-only"> (fewest)</span>}</td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="sc-key">Guilty if: <b>Counterfactual</b>, the offer changed its price; <b>Took part</b>, also the agent that says yes but would have followed anyway; <b>Conduct</b>, ended at B&rsquo;s price without distancing itself; <b>Words</b>, said yes.</p>
  </div>
  <figcaption id={`${uid}-cap`}><slot /></figcaption>
  <details class="data">
    <summary>Show both monitors</summary>
    <div class="sc-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Guilty if&hellip;</th>{rules.map((r) => <th scope="col">{r}</th>)}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map((row) => (
            <tr><th scope="row">{row.name}</th>
              {row.trusted.map((v, i) => <td>{i < 2 ? v : `${v} / ${row.untrusted[i]}`}</td>)}</tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Wrong verdicts out of 268, trusted / untrusted monitor. Price and Replay use no monitor. With the
      untrusted monitor the best rule under &ldquo;took part&rdquo; is the reasoning watcher (6); under the
      counterfactual definition the replay stays best (7, against 65 for the next rule).</p>
  </details>
</figure>
